{
  "description": "C57 lifecycle fault matrix, shared by the TypeScript conformance suite (apps/server/src/sandbox-relay/lifecycle-conformance.pg.test.ts, which drives its host double from these rows) and the Rust daemon suite (apps/cli/src/sandbox_relay/lifecycle_conformance_tests.rs, which asserts the real daemon's restart receipts against them). Each cell is one loss at one boundary in one direction. `host.journal` is the durable phase the host reached before it died (null: never journaled; `delivered`: the result reached the server but the confirmation was lost); `host.effect` says whether the runtime effect happened. `receipt` is what the restarted host reports (null: nothing); `operation` is the server's terminal state; `effects` is how many runtime effects exist at the end, which an uncertain retry under the same key must never raise. `carry` rows (reconnect plan WP3) are relay outages, not deaths: one carried attempt (`phase`: `intent` never started, `effect` issued) and what ends it while the host is disconnected (`ending`: `reconnect`, its own timer, the sandbox lease, `carry_intent_window` or `max_carry`). `decision` is the daemon's per-entry carry rule (apps/cli/src/sandbox_relay/carry.rs asserts it): `keep` carries on, `revoke` settles by its journaled receipt, `stop` cancels the running command through the cancel proof path. `expect.operation` is the server's terminal state (`lease_behaviour`: unchanged lease expiry; `receipt`: whatever its journaled result was); `unprovenStop` is the state when the host cannot prove the stop.",
